{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CetDJqp6qoMwnoRDBcsCe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have a clear understanding of the repository structure. Let me document my findings:\n\n**Requirement restated**: Add a `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` endpoint that transitions a shipment from CREATED to CONFIRMED (idempotent), rejects CANCELLED shipments with 409, and rejects missing shipments with 404.\n\n**Repository findings**:\n- Shipment model: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/Shipment.kt:9-27` with ShipmentStatus enum\n- ShipmentController: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt:20-56` (no confirm endpoint yet)\n- ShipmentRepository: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentRepository.kt:10-27` (in-memory store)\n- Error handling: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiExceptions.kt` with ResourceNotFoundException and ConflictException\n- ErrorCode enum: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiError.kt:31-37`\n\n**Conventions established**:\n- Controllers use `@PostMapping` for state-changing operations\n- `ResourceNotFoundException` with ErrorCode for 404s\n- `ConflictException` with ErrorCode for 409s (state conflicts)\n- GlobalExceptionHandler converts ApiExceptions to ApiError responses\n- Tests use MockMvc and jsonPath assertions\n- Baseline tests (13 total) currently pass\n\n**Affected files**:\n1. `ApiError.kt` – Need new ErrorCode for invalid shipment status\n2. `ShipmentController.kt` – Add the confirm endpoint\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` – Add tests for confirm behavior\n\n**Risks**:\n- Adding new ErrorCode could affect serialization/deserialization\n- Idempotence must work correctly (CONFIRMED→CONFIRMED succeeds)\n- Must distinguish 404 (missing) from 409 (invalid state)\n\n**Open questions**: None that change behavior; the requirement is clear.\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed changes**:\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** – Add `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS` to the ErrorCode enum. This will be thrown when confirming a shipment in an invalid state (CANCELLED).\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** – Add a new endpoint:\n   - `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")`\n   - Takes shipmentId from path\n   - Fetches shipment; throws ResourceNotFoundException if missing\n   - If status is CREATED, transitions to CONFIRMED and saves\n   - If status is CONFIRMED, no-op (idempotent success)\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throws ConflictException with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS\n   - Returns the shipment with 200 OK\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** – Add four new tests:\n   - `confirms a created shipment and returns it in CONFIRMED status`\n   - `retrying confirm of a confirmed shipment succeeds without change`\n   - `rejecting confirm of a cancelled shipment with error envelope and 409`\n   - `rejecting confirm of unknown shipment with error envelope and 404`\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected**: \n- Could add a service layer to separate business logic. Rejected because the existing architecture has controller/repository only, and the ticket says \"preserve existing Kotlin + Spring Boot architecture.\" Adding a service would be architectural change beyond the ticket's scope.\n\n**Data and error flow**:\n\n*Case 1: CREATED → CONFIRMED*\n- Input: POST /shipments/S-1/confirm where S-1 status=CREATED\n- Read: repository.findById(\"S-1\") → Shipment(status=CREATED)\n- Write: repository.save(Shipment(status=CONFIRMED))\n- Return: 200 OK with updated Shipment JSON\n\n*Case 2: Idempotent confirm (CONFIRMED)*\n- Input: POST /shipments/S-1/confirm where S-1 status=CONFIRMED\n- Read: repository.findById(\"S-1\") → Shipment(status=CONFIRMED)\n- Write: repository.save with same status (no-op)\n- Return: 200 OK with Shipment JSON unchanged\n\n*Case 3: CANCELLED shipment*\n- Input: POST /shipments/S-1/confirm where S-1 status=CANCELLED\n- Read: repository.findById(\"S-1\") → Shipment(status=CANCELLED)\n- Throw: ConflictException with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS\n- Return: 409 Conflict with ApiError envelope\n\n*Case 4: Unknown shipment*\n- Input: POST /shipments/S-missing/confirm\n- Read: repository.findById(\"S-missing\") → null\n- Throw: ResourceNotFoundException with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n- Return: 404 Not Found with ApiError envelope\n\n**Test strategy**:\n- Test 1: Create a CREATED shipment, confirm it, verify status changed to CONFIRMED\n- Test 2: Confirm an already CONFIRMED shipment, verify no change and 200 OK\n- Test 3: Create a CANCELLED shipment (write directly to repository), attempt confirm, verify 409 Conflict with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS code\n- Test 4: Attempt confirm on non-existent shipment, verify 404 Not Found with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll implement the changes according to the design."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":395,"cache_read_input_tokens":19956,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":395},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f51f5a32-006c-4516-9e32-203048ae0952","uuid":"65dd1440-32bd-4822-9702-94e5628e1cba","timestamp":"2026-09-09T16:53:00.853Z","request_id":"req_011CetDJqCPNjvAr9sFdV6YL"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CetDJqp6qoMwnoRDBcsCe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01S1NHSfM8G5afNbbxghvCpN","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-8a7c7dbf-ab75-4297-9b11-9bccb53c1bd2/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiError.kt","old_string":"/**\n * The closed set of machine-readable error codes. Clients switch on these, so a code is\n * part of the public API: add one deliberately, never rename one casually.\n */\nenum class ErrorCode {\n    ORDER_NOT_FOUND,\n    ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS,\n    SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND,\n    SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS,\n    VALIDATION_FAILED,\n}","new_string":"/**\n * The closed set of machine-readable error codes. Clients switch on these, so a code is\n * part of the public API: add one deliberately, never rename one casually.\n */\nenum class ErrorCode {\n    ORDER_NOT_FOUND,\n    ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS,\n    SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND,\n    SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS,\n    SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS,\n    VALIDATION_FAILED,\n}"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":395,"cache_read_input_tokens":19956,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":395},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f51f5a32-006c-4516-9e32-203048ae0952","uuid":"13bbebec-7ba9-4dc3-bfc8-3868e46b63cf","timestamp":"2026-09-09T16:53:04.611Z","request_id":"req_011CetDJqCPNjvAr9sFdV6YL"}
